__label__books the theory of everything the origin and fate of the universe from audiofile physicist stephen hawking suffers from amyotrophic lateral sclerosis also known as lou gehrig's disease the condition has progressed to the point where he can no longer speak for himself hawking therefore uses a voice synthesizer to deliver this series of popular lectures on black holes current physics theories and the nature of time and space the synthesizer paces sentences oddly and slurs an occasional word hawking jokes about being unable to get rid of its american accent however listeners will soon adapt to the oddities of delivery and once they do will find themselves inspired by the sweep and clarity of hawking's mind and by his warmth and bravery g t b audiofile 2002 portland maine copyright audiofile portland maine
